I always imagined the story of my first  love would be a magical one not a  cautionary tale I just started college  in Chicago I was so fun and carefree and  feisty I thought I was invincible and  ready to take over the world  I was fearless and then I met him he was  so handsome and charming our first date  was a walk in the park I remember he  pointed out that I had a booger in my  nose and I was super embarrassed he  asked me to be his girlfriend a few  months later and of course I said yes  and that's when things changed I slowly  stopped hanging out with my friends it  was always just me and him and when as  far as him creating a rift and ruining  the trust between my best friend and I  me and her didn't speak for almost two  years he would get upset at me and he  would break my cellphone so I couldn't  talk to anyone he was convinced that I  was cheating on him he would get upset  at me for saying hi to my guy friends on  the street but that should have been  assigned right there he was emotionally  abusive and he made me feel like every  decision I made was wrong  I felt that nothing I did could make him  happy the first time he hit me I was  convinced that it was my fault and that  might attitude made him upset and maybe  if I didn't talk back things would get  better between us the moment I knew that  I had to get out of their relationship  was when he knocked me down and I fell  and I hit my head it wasn't the first  time he hit me but it was the first time  I felt really scared I called my best  friend and I finally told her the truth  and she said she was coming to get me  and I was staying with her in the  suburbs I was packing he came home early  and was livid when he saw that I was  leaving I didn't realize the situation  got out of hand until he pulled a  kitchen knife on me he told me if you  leave me you're gonna kill me so he may  as well kill me now  and only then did my brain register  danger my best friend came at the nick  of time she called the cops  and that's when he slit his wrists the  cops came and took him to the hospital I  felt so guilty I was an empty shell of  myself  I was apologizing for my very existence  I had no voice had no identity I was  seeking approval from everyone except  myself much to my regret I did end up  going back to him a few months later we  were off and on again  there was a tug of war between my  loneliness and depression and  vulnerability I was trying to find peace  with myself and I wanted to forgive him  so I wasn't carrying the hatred that I  felt for him I found myself in an all  too familiar situation but I felt that  he wasn't trying to knock me down to  size again and things with us weren't  really done until about another year and  a half later when he moved to a  different state I always thought how did  this happen to someone like me I was a  good girl I wasn't raised in a household  with domestic abuse  all of my friends had no relationships  what was wrong with me why did he feel  he had to hit me once he was gone for  good  I rediscovered the things that made me  happy again I threw myself into my  career I had new friends and love  interests I had a therapist who I saw  once a week she helped me build myself  back together again if you're going  through this I want you to know to pay  attention to the signs it's hard because  your emotions are clouded and you're in  love the love is supposed to make you  feel good you should always lift you up  listen to your friends they care don't  forget that you are still a good person  because you deserve all the happiness in  the world and you're worth it
 

